---

<section id="accessibility" class="py-20 w-full" style="scroll-margin-top: 80px; background-color: #171717; color: #ffffff;">
	<div class="w-full px-lg" style="margin: 0 auto; max-width: 80rem;">
		<div class="mb-12">
			<h2 class="text-display-lg mb-4">Accessibility is not optional.</h2>
			<p class="text-body-lg">
				1.3 billion people worldwide have disabilities. Ensuring color contrast isn't just ethical—it's
				good business. Users with low vision, color blindness, and other visual impairments need your
				interface to be accessible.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 mb-12">
			<div>
				<div class="text-5xl font-semibold mb-2">1.3B</div>
				<p class="text-body-lg" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);">People with disabilities globally</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<div class="text-5xl font-semibold mb-2">$6.9T</div>
				<p class="text-body-lg" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);">Spending power of disabled population</p>
			</div>

			<div>
				<div class="text-5xl font-semibold mb-2">25%</div>
				<p class="text-body-lg" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);">Of web users experience vision challenges</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="rounded-lg p-8" style="background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);">
			<h3 class="text-display-sm mb-4">Legal Requirements</h3>
			<p class="text-body-md mb-4" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);">
				Accessible design is legally mandated under:
			</p>
			<ul class="space-y-2 text-body-md" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);">
				<li>• <strong>WCAG 2.2</strong> — Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (globally adopted)</li>
				<li>• <strong>ADA Title III</strong> — Americans with Disabilities Act (US)</li>
				<li>• <strong>EN 301 549</strong> — European accessibility standard</li>
				<li>• <strong>AODA</strong> — Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (Canada)</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
